(EXP-25: `{x add y} multiply z` - curly braces group a subexpression and
 override the default precedence.
 Also covers: EXP-28, the instruction to brace each complex subexpression.
 The first line is the same expression unbraced, so the pair records what the
 grouping actually changes: 2 add 3 multiply 4 is 14, braced it is 20.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-25.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   14
   20
   6
)
a number called x is 2.
a number called y is 3.
a number called z is 4.
Print x add y multiply z.
Print {x add y} multiply z.
Print {{x add y} multiply z} modulo 7.
